(Was: cyclic list structure is depth-bounded, not stack-overflowing - plan
 040 stage 1e1 acceptance 5, pinning `append x to x` as a genuine
 self-referential cycle, truncated by `_list_print`'s 64-deep guard.
 docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111 (owner ruling, GitHub #34, Option 1): a
 collection placed inside another collection is now a COPY, so `append x
 to x` copies x's state at the moment of the append (here, `[]`) and
 appends that copy - it can no longer construct a real cycle. `x` ends up
 holding one element, an empty list, not itself.)

a list called x is [].
append x to x.
print x.
on error print "E".
